    {
        "content": "<p>I have two remarks about the <code>invalidField</code> error. First, the second paragraph of  <a href=\"https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/4.33.1/Error-Explanations/About___--invalidField/#lean___invalidField\">the documentation</a> is a bit mangled. More importantly, I rather frequently hit</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Invalid field `bar`: The environment does not contain `Exists.bar`</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>where I would rather expect to see <code>Invalid field `bar`: The environment does not contain `Foo.bar` </code></p>",
        "id": 625260334,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1789742144
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The latter is about reducibility, right? E.g. if <code>Foo</code> were <code>irreducible</code>, that's what would appear in the error?</p>",
        "id": 625260986,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1789742301
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sure, but the error message could start with mentioning <code>Foo</code> before unfolding and mentioning <code>Exists</code>.</p>",
